<html><head>
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8"></head><body>Adele,<br><br>Effective immediately, I'm implementing a dual-authorization requirement for all outgoing wire transfers exceeding $10,000.<br><br>The new process:<br>1. The requestor completes the Wire Transfer Authorization Form (I'll have it on the shared drive by end of day under Finance &gt; Forms)<br>2. The form must be signed by the requestor AND a second authorized signer<br>3. Authorized signers are: myself, Grady, and Nestor<br>4. The bank will require verbal confirmation from one of the authorized signers before processing any wire over $25,000<br><br>This is in response to industry-wide increases in payment fraud targeting manufacturers. Our bank (Columbia Bank) has also been recommending this for commercial accounts.<br><br>I know it adds a step, but it's a necessary safeguard. Please update your AP procedures accordingly.<br><br>Patti Fernandez<br>CFO<br>Waverly Industrial Solutions, Inc.</body></html>

